# Docker & Deployment

## Images (per app — no root Dockerfile)

| App    | Dockerfile               | Start                                  | Health            |
| ------ | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------- | ----------------- |
| api    | `apps/api/Dockerfile`    | `node apps/api/dist/main.js`           | `/live`, `/ready` |
| worker | `apps/worker/Dockerfile` | `node apps/worker/dist/main.js`        | `/live`, `/ready` |
| web    | `apps/web/Dockerfile`    | `node apps/web/server.js` (standalone) | `/healthz`        |

Build pattern: `turbo prune <app> --docker` → pnpm install → build → `pnpm deploy --prod`.

Node **24**, pnpm via corepack. Production runs as non-root (`nestjs`, `worker`, `nextjs`).

## Compose files

| File                               | Use                                                         |
| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docker-compose.yml`               | Local: Postgres 17, Redis 8, MinIO, Mailpit                 |
| `docker-compose.dokploy.yml`       | Production stack (migrate job + api + worker + web + infra) |
| `docker-compose.observability.yml` | Prometheus scrape config                                    |
| `deploy/docker-stack.swarm.yml`    | Secondary Swarm + Traefik path                              |

**Primary prod path:** Dokploy Compose (`docker-compose.dokploy.yml`), not Nixpacks.

## Dokploy notes

- One Compose app; build context = repo root.
- Secrets in Dokploy Environment UI → `.env` for compose interpolation.
- Required: `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `REDIS_PASSWORD`, `MINIO_ROOT_USER`, `MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD`.
- Do **not** set `REDIS_URL` in Dokploy UI for in-compose Redis — compose builds it from `REDIS_PASSWORD`.
- Traefik labels on `web` and `api`; worker is internal only.
- `migrate` service runs `docker-entrypoint.migrate.sh` before api/worker start.

## Web build args

`NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars must be passed as Docker `--build-arg` (baked at build time).

## Ask before changing

Dockerfiles, compose files, Swarm stack, or deployment env wiring — unless explicitly requested.
